--- !u!114 &1004194158
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1004194153}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4dffc53fb88cadd43934a5280ec0f29b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  newspapers:
  - newspaper: {fileID: 2130458222}
    innerMonologueText: 'This is from a foreign paper. They have no government stake
      here.

'
    believeText: ndependent observers. No reason to fabricate.
    questionText: Could be biased against Marcos.
    lessonTitle: Documented widespread irregularities
    lessonDescription: "Foreign observers including a U.S. delegation documented
      widespread irregularities \u2014 ballot stuffing, voter intimidation, and suspicious
      tally discrepancies. Their reports were among the most credible sources of
      the period precisely because they had no local political stake."
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d054cee54ba95d44e9be1fa3bb9ae3c9, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b71e9fedb4d3b5842a5c12db8f2dbff3, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d7414d8202c6a434683d6bd736afa380, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1756386562}
    innerMonologueText: All regions. By the exact same margin. That's not how elections
      work.
    believeText: COMELEC is the official body.
    questionText: ' Uniform results across all regions is a statistical red flag.'
    lessonTitle: Marcos-owned Publication
    lessonDescription: "The Times Journal was a Marcos-owned publication. Uniform
      leads across all regions are statistically implausible in any genuine election
      \u2014 different communities vote differently based on local conditions and
      loyalties."
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee4c431aedeec9b4cb9d8a873a45caf8, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4184dd287de2db84da102107f1f41c1e, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2b0574026aafde44487530e6b028a264, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1474734789}
    innerMonologueText: Half a million citizens choosing to spend their day watching
      ballot boxes. That's a real number.
    believeText: That scale of citizen action is verifiable.
    questionText: Could be exaggerated.
    lessonTitle: NAMFREL VOLUNTEERS
    lessonDescription: NAMFREL's mobilization of volunteer watchers was one of the
      most significant civic actions of the period. Their parallel count became the
      most trusted independent tally of the election.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1d498f77ce33d214ebe4450f698f72c0, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5ba3483032f59a14680e235c4bb2eac5, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3a0c5f247bcd21f4aa5cdc7b4554c017, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 827242588}
    innerMonologueText: "'Documents show' \u2014 but where are the documents? Who
      verified them?"
    believeText: Serious allegation. Could be true.
    questionText: Unverified. Same paper called every opposition figure a communist.
    lessonTitle: Another Marcos-Controlled Publication
    lessonDescription: The Daily Express was a Marcos-controlled publication. The
      'communist funding' accusation was a standard tactic used against all opposition
      figures regardless of evidence. No credible documentation was ever produced.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9a2bf40a9b100c14b96af339eb6cdc66, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f5a38a919ebd0114f985a28167d2eb45, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4cae0e0d7fbecf740a7f2c43c00854ca, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 773760861}
    innerMonologueText: ' Government employees walking out of their own jobs, on
      live television. That''s not something you do lightly.'
    believeText: This is a documented, filmed event.
    questionText: They could have been paid by the opposition.
    lessonTitle: COMELEC Computer Operator Walkout
    lessonDescription: The COMELEC computer operator walkout is one of the most documented
      events of the 1986 election. Employees walked out live on television, stating
      they could not continue entering numbers that did not match the actual count.
      It is not a contested event.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c1167d48ef6b5234d8f01e6ddc1c8838, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7bc0b39c823b7c0468ac02300f973692, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 55a1a56761c69dc42a756e27deef6a1e, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 641651971}
    innerMonologueText: No incidents. Anywhere. In a contested national election.
    believeText: Official government report.
    questionText: '''No incidents'' contradicts every independent observer''s report.'
    lessonTitle: Incidents During Election
    lessonDescription: Independent observers documented hundreds of incidents including
      ballot box snatching, voter intimidation, and precinct closures. A government
      gazette claiming zero incidents contradicts all outside reporting.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: db73a9b1ed2f4cb4dbed3f785b73f72e, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a4b9601e0ed515547874c6b0c48671b8, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 110b241a43a7b9746abfc5298c9edce0, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1651901888}
    innerMonologueText: Ordinary people using their bodies to protect a ballot box.
      That's not something you coordinate as propaganda.
    believeText: Specific location, specific action. Verifiable.
    questionText: Could be staged.
    lessonTitle: Ballot Protection
    lessonDescription: Spontaneous citizen ballot protection actions occurred in
      multiple provinces. The Philippine Daily Inquirer was one of the few independent
      papers still operating. Specific, local, verifiable events reported with named
      locations are among the most credible categories of reporting.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ac68a9ea2cb1c864a82879f63e9d57ac, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 637ac0de5b5d3864db3e79edb17102c8, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c62f98b539b0bee42bc46b78f372d4dd, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1515174895}
    innerMonologueText: '  A foreign regional publication. Covers Southeast Asia.
      No local political stake.'
    believeText: ' Independent regional press. Consistent with other reporting.'
    questionText: Could be anti-Marcos bias.
    lessonTitle: Aquino Rallies
    lessonDescription: The Far Eastern Economic Review was an independent Hong Kong-based
      publication with no alignment to either side. Large rally attendance was documented
      by multiple independent observers across the country.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 16bbef1587e466b40935ab1d6e0b4497, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b61165a7d9e029e4ab4622671cec8b98, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 64ac1b953a425e343bfb2b216f7ecb62, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1456193943}
    innerMonologueText: ' A government publication saying the government is democratic.

'
    believeText: Could be genuine.
    questionText: State-run media praising the state is not independent reporting.
    lessonTitle: ' Another Marcos-Controlled Publication'
    lessonDescription: Bagong Lipunan News was a Marcos regime publication. A state-run
      outlet affirming the legitimacy of a state-run election is not an independent
      source. The source of a claim matters as much as the claim itself.
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f5dc19ceb29c99744aca977f1e5fd31f, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6db222d1a9d39f5428fd09fcd2378f8f, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9c05c30f8131f794fa31df539f4894b0, type: 3}
  - newspaper: {fileID: 1218378062}
    innerMonologueText: 'Two bodies. Two counts. Two winners. Same election.

'
    believeText: One of these is the real count.
    questionText: One of these is fabricated.
    lessonTitle: ' Two Tallies'
    lessonDescription: "Both counts were released publicly. They cannot both be correct.
      The NAMFREL count was generated by independent citizen observers with no government
      control over their tallies. The COMELEC count was produced by the government
      body responsible for announcing the result. The question of which number was
      real is not a matter of opinion \u2014 it is a matter of evidence."
    innerMonologueSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0c68fae3e96b747488ef8ec9e81decd4, type: 3}
    believeSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ffa08c30fd408b04fa9274176537ca13, type: 3}
    questionSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 76e8f63316c4a4a469b2a1b708276166, type: 3}
  questPanel: {fileID: 84965258}
  innerMonologuePanel: {fileID: 840340188}
  choicesPanel: {fileID: 1409144636}
  lessonPanel: {fileID: 171240785}
  innerMonologueText: {fileID: 1498896188}
  believeBtn: {fileID: 1735668087}
  questionBtn: {fileID: 1627502336}
  lessonTitleText: {fileID: 1507880664}
  lessonDescriptionText: {fileID: 1370061929}
  tapAnywhereBtn: {fileID: 322060976}
  huds:
  - {fileID: 105302947}
  - {fileID: 270139073}
  endPanel: {fileID: 963839919}
  levelCompleteManager: {fileID: 1138115188}
  newspaperSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5dd44e77c60e7204eb55e58e107c943f, type: 3}
